  "body": "I have already submitted this in the matrix admin support channel and it got blank stares, I have a hunch something fucky is going on: \r\n\r\nhi folks, im running a private server will small userbase, I have a very weird issue where one specific user in a room cannot see one other specific users messages (its just showing \"waiting for message ect\")  \r\n\r\n- the issue is one way, \r\n- member B cant see Member A's messages, \r\n- everyone else can see both members messages and Member A can see Member B's messages\r\n\r\n\r\nthe only thing out of the ordinary is Member A has moderator roll in the one channel this is happening in, in another channel where neither of them have moderator Member A can read Member B's messages\r\n\r\nim at my wits end, no one ive talked to has seen this before and I've already tried having member B rejoin the channel \r\nI can try completely wiping the channel, remaking it and not assigning anyone moderator but if that works there is still some underlying issue im dodging which I don't get at all \r\n\r\nive also had Member A open a direct message with member B which works fine \r\nthe exact message placeholder that Member A sees is \"Waiting for this message, this may take a while.\" \r\n\r\nboth Member A and B are using element on android \r\n\r\nall other members of both channels can see member A and B msgs no problem",
